You could tell inla to produce fitted.values on the natural scale, by setting link=1 (in control.predictor). (The rinla.org <http://rinla.org> FAQ entry is called something like “how do I make predictions with INLA?”)
I don’t have an explanation for why you appear to get reasonable values without applying the link function.

Finn

